Package: argus-tty
Version: __VERSION__
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Ram Laxman Yadav <yadavramlaxman@gmail.com>
Depends: openssh-server, sudo, passwd, bsdutils, e2fsprogs, curl, logrotate, systemd, acl
Suggests: awscli, libpam-google-authenticator
Homepage: https://github.com/ramlaxmanyadav/argus-tty
Description: SSH session auditing and tiered sudo access control for Linux fleets
 Provisions real per-user Linux accounts across three tiers — developer,
 admin, deployer — each with its own scoped sudo whitelist, and forces
 every SSH session through a TTY and command-history recorder. No shared
 root/deploy account, so every command is attributable to the person who
 ran it.
 .
 Session recordings ship to S3 and connect/disconnect email alerts go out
 through a privilege-separated SMTP mailer — both optional and
 non-blocking; sessions always record locally first, and neither ever
 holds a login open. Optional Google Authenticator (TOTP) two-factor
 authentication is also available for developer/admin sessions, and the
 tier names themselves are customizable.
 .
 Installs as a single .deb: `apt install` across a fleet instead of
 hand-rolling sshd_config + PAM + a TTY recorder per box.
 .
 Full configuration reference, architecture notes, and source:
 https://github.com/ramlaxmanyadav/argus-tty
 .
 Run `sudo argus-tty status` after install to check configuration.
